      "headline": "Senior backend dev, sometime team lead, sometimes architect.",
      "about": "Hi.\n\nCurrently work at Medtronic as an embedded software engineer and dev lead (C++, software architect) and also platform dev (Python mainly). Writing tools to maintain video streaming devices within operating theatres.\n\nI recently a senior engineer at Sensat, helping to develop a visualisation platform for the building industry. Worked combining 3D graphics with GIS (Three.js, Typescript, WebGL), in particular viewing pointclouds. Often called in to help out on other code in Pulumi, Typescript and Golang.\n\nPast roles have also been as lead/senior developer in start ups as they transition to stable companies. My knowledge is mainly in system building, but also in programming languages, testing, databases, code quality and high discipline agile developments.\n\nRecent-ish examples of work include scaling infrastructure globally, 3D graphics, GIS, terabyte scale social media, petabyte video storage and rendering, software architecture, and some lower level coding in C down to PIC chips.\n\nFor side projects I was the co-founder and in past times president of the PHP London organisation, founder of the UK PHP conference, creator or co-creator of several open source projects (CGreen, SimpleTest, Phemto), authored regular programming columns and an occasional technical book reviewer. Co-author/contributer to Manning's \"PHP in Action\" and contributer to O'Reilly's \"97 things every programmer should know\".\n\nWas a very early implementer of agile methods, starting with eXtreme Programming in 2001.\n\nKnown as \"lastcraft\" on the developer forums.\n\nyours, Marcus\n\nSpecialties: lead developer, previously web developer, now database developer, object oriented analysis and design, scrum master, agile development.\nBuzzwords that tell you next to nothing: Typescript, C, SQL, Python, Ruby, PHP, Perl, Scheme, UML, XP, Scrum, Postgres, MySQL, Mongo, three.js,  pulumi, AWS.",
